        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-c8b824f5b1@example.invalid",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-c8b824f5b1@example.invalid",
          "jcr:created": "Fri Oct 28 2022 15:17:21 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<p>The SEA team of more than 40 people (employees and family members) helped to plant a combination of 100 oak trees and bushes. The red, white and bur oak trees will grow well together with the hazelnut bushes to reclaim the former farmland. Brian Ecklund, Senior Staff Engineer, and a SEA member said, “It’s great to be a part of a really meaningful activity that engages such a wide range of people – both young and old.”</p>\n<p>This event is an example of our employees putting their commitment into action to help make a positive impact on the local community. “It was so much fun to see all the kids digging in the dirt and taking pictures by “their” trees,” said Jan Sahm, Staff Project Specialist Quality Operations and SEA site lead. “Not only are we helping improve the environment, but we’re educating our children about the importance of being lifelong caretakers of our planet,” she said.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Oct 28 2022 15:45:13 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        },
